{"name":"Toffee Tart","hex":"#c08950","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"toffee","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of chewy confectionery made by boiling sugar (or treacle, etc) with butter or milk, then cooling the mixture so that it becomes hard.","A small, individual piece of toffee."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To coat in toffee."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/toffee"},{"term":"tart","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Sharp to the taste; acid; sour.","High or too high in acidity."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of small open pie, or piece of pastry, now typically containing jelly (US) / jam (UK) or conserve, or sometimes other fillings (chocolate, custard, egg, butter, historically even meat or other savory fillings).","A melt (block of wax for use in a tart burner)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tart"}],"entries":[{"title":"Toffee","blocks":[{"text":"Toffee is an English confection made by caramelizing sugar or molasses along with butter, and occasionally flour. The mixture is heated until its temperature reaches the hard crack stage of 149 to 154 °C. While being prepared, toffee is sometimes mixed with nuts or raisins."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Thorntonstoffee.jpg/330px-Thorntonstoffee.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Toffee"},{"title":"Tart","blocks":[{"text":"A tart is a baked dish consisting of a filling over a pastry base with an open top not covered with pastry. The pastry is usually shortcrust pastry; the filling may be sweet or savoury, though modern tarts are usually fruit-based, sometimes with custard. Tartlet refers to a miniature tart; an example would be egg tarts. The categories of \"tart\", \"flan\", and \"pie\" overlap, with no sharp distinctions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Raspberry_tart.jpg/330px-Raspberry_tart.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tart"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Heath-broken.JPG/500px-Heath-broken.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Heath-broken.JPG/1280px-Heath-broken.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Heath-broken.JPG/500px-Heath-broken.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Heath candy bar, which is English toffee coated in milk chocolate ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHeath-broken.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Akashi_City_Museum_of_Culture_Hyogo_pref_Japan13s.jpg/500px-Akashi_City_Museum_of_Culture_Hyogo_pref_Japan13s.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Akashi_City_Museum_of_Culture_Hyogo_pref_Japan13s.jpg/1280px-Akashi_City_Museum_of_Culture_Hyogo_pref_Japan13s.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Akashi_City_Museum_of_Culture_Hyogo_pref_Japan13s.jpg/500px-Akashi_City_Museum_of_Culture_Hyogo_pref_Japan13s.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Piece of apple tart","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAkashi_City_Museum_of_Culture_Hyogo_pref_Japan13s.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/00_Lemon_Meringue_Tarts.jpg/500px-00_Lemon_Meringue_Tarts.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/00_Lemon_Meringue_Tarts